From: Akos Seres <seresakos2000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:08:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: nvgpu: clean up failed system-memory allocations
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Match the allocation and free helpers when NVGPU_MM_BYPASSES_IOMMU is
enabled, as it is on Xavier. The non-contiguous allocation returns a
pages array, so its failure path must use nvgpu_dma_free_no_iommu(),
matching the normal free path. Clear the saved pages pointer afterward.

Also release any partial scatterlist state before freeing its container.

Adapted for OE4T linux-nvgpu d530a48d64f9ad3020d9f3307f53e8dde8e3fba1.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Akos Seres <seresakos2000@gmail.com>

diff --git a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/linux-dma.c b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/linux-dma.c
--- a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/linux-dma.c
+++ b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/linux-dma.c
@@ -328,7 +328,11 @@ fail_free_sgt:
 	nvgpu_free_sgtable(g, &mem->priv.sgt);
 fail_free_dma:
-	dma_free_attrs(d, size, alloc_ret, iova, dma_attrs);
+	if (nvgpu_nvlink_non_contig(g, flags))
+		nvgpu_dma_free_no_iommu(size, alloc_ret);
+	else
+		dma_free_attrs(d, size, alloc_ret, iova, dma_attrs);
 	mem->cpu_va = NULL;
+	mem->priv.pages = NULL;
 	mem->priv.sgt = NULL;
 	mem->size = 0;
 	g->dma_memory_used -= size;
@@ -642,2 +646,4 @@ int nvgpu_get_sgtable_from_pages(struct gk20a *g, struct sg_table **sgt,
-	if (tbl)
+	if (tbl) {
+		sg_free_table(tbl);
 		nvgpu_kfree(g, tbl);
+	}
